Reason: an instance deactivated before the collision grid's first sync was skipped by it and never given cells;
waking it only flipped `active`, so grid queries (position_meeting, collision_point, place_meeting) could not see it
until the room was left. AM2R deactivates every solid beyond the view as a room starts, so ledges and slopes away from
where Samus entered lost their ledge grab and spider-ball grip.
Upstream: Engine bug on every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

diff --git a/src/runner.h b/src/runner.h
--- a/src/runner.h
+++ b/src/runner.h
@@ -993,7 +993,12 @@
     (void)runner;
 #endif
 
+    bool waking = active && !instance->active;
     instance->active = active;
+    // AM2R deactivates far solids as a room starts, before the grid's first sync, so they never got cells: list them again
+    // as they wake, or position_meeting and collision_point (ledge grabs, spider ball) never see them.
+    if (waking && arrlen(instance->collisionCells) == 0 && runner->spatialGrid != nullptr)
+        SpatialGrid_markInstanceAsDirty(runner->spatialGrid, instance);
 }
 
